      "id": "tjtsxhz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of National Income"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Gross Domestic Product (GDP) measures the total monetary value of final goods and services produced strictly within the domestic boundary of a nation.",
        "Gross National Product (GNP) adjusts GDP by adding Net Factor Income from Abroad (NFIA), reflecting income earned by residents globally.",
        "Net National Product (NNP) at factor cost is officially considered the true National Income of an economy.",
        "National income is measured using three distinct approaches: Product/Value Added Method, Income Method, and Expenditure Method.",
        "In India, official estimation was initiated under the National Income Committee (1949) headed by Prof. P.C. Mahalanobis and is currently compiled by the NSO."
      ],
      "id": "3kbpb2b"
    },
